    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0748" n="728" xml:id="pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/9–1450</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">United States Delegation Minutes: SFM Min–4</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>New York</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1950-09-14T15:00:00-04:00">September 14, 1950, 3:00 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg><anchor n="1" xml:id="d513-f1"/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Conference of the United States, United Kingdom, and
                        French Foreign Ministers</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York, September</hi> 1950</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">minutes of the fourth meeting held in the
                        waldorf-astoria 3:00 p. m. september 14, 1950</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Members</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">Mr. Acheson (US)</p>
                <p rendition="#center">Mr. Schuman (FR)</p>
                <p rendition="#center">Mr. Bevin (UK)</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Present</hi>
                </p>
                <table cols="3" rows="5">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">United States</hi>
                        </cell>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">France</hi>
                        </cell>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">United Kingdom</hi>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Philip C. Jessup</cell>
                        <cell>Henri Bonnet</cell>
                        <cell>M. E. Dening</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>George W. Perkins</cell>
                        <cell>Jean Chauvel</cell>
                        <cell>Sir Pierson Dixon</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Dean Rusk</cell>
                        <cell>M. de Latournelle</cell>
                        <cell>Sir Oliver Franks</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Roland de Margerie</cell>
                        <cell>Sir Gladwyn Jebb</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Korea</hi>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Acheson</hi> noted that the UN delegations of
                    the three countries had been in constant consultation on the Korean question and
                    were agreed upon the course to be followed in the U.N.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d513-f2"/> Unless there were questions to be raised, it seemed
                    unnecessary to discuss the issue further.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Bevin</hi> said that at a later time the United
                    Kingdom wished to discuss the attitude to be taken toward the Syngman Rhee
                    government, but there was no need to raise the issue now.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d513-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d513-f1" n="1" xml:id="d513-f1-content">
                <p>The complete text of these minutes is scheduled for publication in volume <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d513-f2" n="2" xml:id="d513-f2-content">
                <p>See the memorandum agreed upon by the three U.N. delegations dated September 6,
                        <ref target="#pg704">p. 704</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d513-f3" n="3" xml:id="d513-f3-content">
                <p>The U.S. Delegation Summary Minutes of this portion of the meeting read as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>“Mr. Acheson noted that the Delegations of the three governments to the United
                    Nations had had a full exchange of views on the subject of Korea and were fully
                    agreed upon the course to be followed in the United Nations with respect to that
                    problem.</p>
                <p>“The Ministers <hi rendition="#italic">approved</hi> the understanding reached by
                    their Delegations in this matter.” (Summary Minutes 4:795.00/9–1450)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
